I arrive at Nele's flat building.
The building is beautiful and has a large wooden door.
I carefully carry the small box in both hands.
I read the names on the door and ring the bell.
Shortly afterwards I hear Nele's voice from the speaker.
"Maya, I will open the door for you right away," Nele says.
The door clicks and I push it open.
I walk up the stairs to the second floor.
Nele is already standing at her flat door and smiles.
"Hello Maya, it is so nice that you are here!" she says.
"Hello Nele, thank you for the invitation," I answer.
I give her the box from the bakery.
"I have brought you a dessert," I say.
Nele takes the box and beams.
"Oh, a fruit tart, thank you very much!" she says.
I am happy that she likes the cake.
"Come in, I will show you my flat," she says.
I follow her into the warm hallway.
